            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0323" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg315"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.24/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-25T23:00:00-05:00">October 25, 1941—11
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>604. Your 1591 of October 15, 3 p.m. Hopkins has advised as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“With reference to giving aid to Egypt under Lend-Lease, it is not
                            believed that any commitment should be undertaken at this time. The
                            situation is complex and the attitude of the British will have to be
                            ascertained. Furthermore, all available shipping and supplies are badly
                            needed by the British, the Russians and the Chinese.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
